# Lámsza network consistency

`lamsza/docs/network/UI_BASELINE.md` is the source: the owner's decision for each shared element (tokens, CSS rules, toolbar, footer, icons, dialogs, settings, error pages, sign-in, admin), naming which app's version is the baseline. For anything it does not cover, match lamsza.com. A dictionary or a game may add its own pages. It does not invent a second look.

Before adding or changing a shared control, look it up in `UI_BASELINE.md`, then open the baseline app's version and match it. A change to a baseline element is made in every app that has it (WAYS_OF_WORKING R3).

- Dev frontends stay on the fixed ports of `start-lamsza-network.sh` (WAYS_OF_WORKING §1) with `strictPort: true`. If that port is not free, do not start the app on another port.
- Theme uses `data-theme` and the `theme` localStorage key (`light`, `dark`, `system`). Vanilla CSS. No Tailwind, Material, or a new font, color, or card system.
- Toolbar: left side is the app's sections, icon plus visible name. Right side is account and settings, icon only. The name goes in `title` and `<span class="sr-only">`, the same way Lámsza does **Belépés** and **Kijelentkezés**.
- Icons come from the one shared set, `AppIcon.svelte` (24 viewBox, stroke 2, round caps), drawn at 16×16 in the toolbar. Do not draw a toolbar icon inline or give one its own size.
- Hungarian UI. Reuse Lámsza's wording for the same action.
- Belépés is a dialog, not its own page. Copy `SignInDialog`: title Belépés, the line `Jelentkezz be a Google-fiókoddal, hogy ki tudd használni a {app name} teljes funkcióit és lehetőségeit.`, then `A Lámsza hálózat alkalmazása. A belépés csak ezen az oldalon jelentkeztet be.` with one link, Irányelvek (`/iranyelvek` on Lámsza; on the other apps `lamszaUrl('/iranyelvek')` from `networkOrigins.js`, which is localhost or `lamsza.test` in dev and lamsza.com only in production), a centered Google button, and Mégse underneath.
- Footer, two centered rows, Játszótér spacing (`.footer-bottom` gap `1em`; `.social-links` and `.policy-links` gap `0.75rem`). Line one: `Sok ❤️-el Székelyföldről. © 2009 - {current year} • {this app's name and description}`. 2009 is the network's first launch. Line two: Facebook, Twitter, Instagram only when the main app admin saved a URL (`social_links` from the matching Lámsza's `/api/config/public`, resolved with `lamszaUrl()` from `networkOrigins.js`; in dev that is localhost or `lamsza.test`, never lamsza.com), each `target="_blank"`. Irányelvek, Adatvédelem, Feltételek, and Sütik exist once, on lamsza.com; every app links those four there (`lamszaUrl()`). Then this app's own `v{version} - Változásnapló`.

```svelte
<!-- ❌ visible label on an account button -->
<button class="btn nav-btn" title="Belépés"><svg>...</svg><span>Belépés</span></button>

<!-- ✅ icon, tooltip, screen-reader name -->
<button class="btn nav-btn" title="Belépés"><svg>...</svg><span class="sr-only">Belépés</span></button>
```

- lamsza-admin is a back office: it has no public toolbar or footer, but it keeps the Hungarian UI, the shared design tokens and the `SignInDialog` (owner decision, 2026-10-07).

This file is canonical in `lamsza/.cursor/rules/`. Do not edit the copies in the other repos: change it here and run `lamsza/scripts/sync-cursor-rules.sh` (WAYS_OF_WORKING R11). A new Lámsza app is added to that script's list.
